// This section is for notes taken in the game.
// THESE SHOULD NEVER GET USED BY THE RUMOR OPCODE
// start at 40000

{40000}{I encountered a strange old man on the outskirts of Shrouded Hills}

{40020}{}

{40040}{}

{40060}{}

{40080}{}

{40100}{}

{40120}{I found a purchase order for a signet ring.  The order was made by a Benjamin Bates, but the ring was purchased for his son, Gilbert Bates.}

{40140}{I found a receipt for goods purchased from P. Schuyler & Sons in Ristezze's file cabinet.  The address is in the city of Tarant.}

{40160}{}

{40180}{}

{40200}{}

{40220}{}

{40240}{A strange shrine at the crash site had this carved into it:  "And His spirit will be reborn on wings of fire in hills shrouded in fog. Archaeon 5:16"}

{40260}{It seems as if only I have survived the crash of the I.F.S. Zephyr. The zeppelin was unexpectedly set upon by strange flying machines. Among the wreckage I found a dying gnome who gave me a signet ring and bid me to find the boy who owned it, with a vague warning of something that "is almost here". He also said that he had "escaped", but I have no clues as to where he escaped from.}

{40280}{I have identified the dead gnome as Preston Radcliffe, from the ticket he had in his pocket.}

{40300}{Buried underneath the wreckage of one of the bizarre flying machines responsible for downing the Zephyr, I have located a dead Orc. Unbelievably, he seems to have been the pilot of the craft. I also found an amulet bearing an eye within a hexagram on his person.}

{40320}{Preston Radcliffe was not a gnome, but a dwarf named Stennar Rock Cutter. For some unknown reason, he did the unthinkable - he cut off his beard simply to pass as a gnome. He must have starved himself as well to make himself appear more gnomish.}

{40340}{Gilbert Bates, the industrialist, seemed to feel some need to unburden his conscience by telling me his deepest secret. He developed his first steam engine from a Black Mountain Clan dwarven prototype which he improved upon. He did not invent it, as everyone had assumed. He feels this youthful indiscretion of his led to the disappearance of the Black Mountain Clan somehow, and is anxious to find out what really happened to them. He was warned by mysterious robed figures in the night to never speak of his association with the Black Mountainers, or the fact that he used their engine to develop his own.} 

{40360}{Gilbert Bates has sent me to Ashbury to look up a sea captain named Edward Teach, an "associate" of Bates that handles "special" jobs for him. He sounds like some sort of pirate, to me. He is meant to ferry me to the Isle of Despair, a penal colony.} 

{40380}{Gilbert Bates has had an attempt made on his life by an assassin wearing the sign of the Molochean Hand, the eye in the hexagram. The Molochean Hand was an order of assassins 500 years ago, and they are thought to have long since disappeared. Bates was not certain whether the would be assassin was a true servant of the Molochean Hand or not.} 

{40400}{I was attacked by someone wearing an amulet bearing the eye in the hexagram symbol, similar to the one that I found on the Orc in the wreckage of the flying machine.}

{40420}{I was attacked by someone wearing an amulet bearing the image of an eye within a hexagram.}

{40440}{}

{40460}{}

{40480}{}

{40500}{}

{40520}{}

{40540}{}

{40560}{}

{40580}{}

{40600}{Upon questioning him of the strange signet ring, Constable Owens told me that Ristezze the Importer might have further information about its origins.}

{40620}{Ristezze the Importer told me that P. Schuyler & Sons is located at 44 Devonshire Way in the city of Tarant, and marked my map accordingly.}

{40640}{I met a dwarf named Magnus Shale Fist loitering outside of P. Schuyler & Sons.  He had some strange theories about their business practices.}

{40660}{Magnus and I have decided to cooperate while investigating P. Schuyler & Sons.  It seems that he's come across a bracelet that purportedly comes from his lost clan.}

{40680}{I found an ancient dwarven tomb deep beneath P. Schuyler & Sons.  I believe they are using its resources for their business.}

{40700}{I found the three Schuyler brothers-Winston, Niles and Edward-on the lowest level of the dwarven tomb.  Theirs is an old family of Necromancers who use their powers to locate valuable and rare items.}

{40720}{I agreed to keep silent about the business operations of P. Schuyler & Sons in return for the identity of the owner of the signet ring.}

{40740}{I agreed to keep silent about the business operations of P. Schuyler & Sons in return for the identity of the owner of the signet ring.  Unfortunately, Magnus was unhappy about it, and was lost in the ensuing battle.}

{40760}{Pelonious Schuyler, the long-dead father of the Winston and his brothers, was called back from the dead in order to answer my question about the ring.  He rambled incoherently for a few moments and then divulged the owner's name-a Mr. Gilbert Bates.}

{40780}{I met a sea captain named Edward Teach.  He told me his ship was for hire, but only through permission of Gilbert Bates.}

